# Which components `make up` starts. THE one knob for this environment.
#
# Compose reads this file automatically and every service is tagged with profiles, so changing this
# single line changes what runs — no edits to docker-compose.yml, and no commented-out blocks
# drifting out of date (R11).
#
#   Value        Components                                    Approx. RAM   Needed from
#   ----------   -------------------------------------------   -----------   -----------------
#   core         Kafka, PostgreSQL, Redis                       ~1.1 GiB      build steps 1-5
#   obs          Zipkin, Prometheus                             ~0.5 GiB      build step 2 (trace check only), formally step 8
#   full         core + obs + Elasticsearch                     ~3.1 GiB      build step 6 onward
#
# Values combine, and the result is the union: `core,obs` runs five services (~1.6 GiB) — useful
# for tracing work without paying for Elasticsearch.
#
# WHY step 2 already needs `obs`, ahead of its "build step 8" column above: `core` alone is enough
# for every one of that step's own success criteria except one — SC-012, quickstart scenario S6 —
# which asks whether an accepting request and the outbox relay's later publish share ONE connected
# trace. Answering that means actually looking at a trace, and Zipkin is what step 2 uses to look.
# `COMPOSE_PROFILES=core,obs` is what that one scenario needs; every other scenario in that step
# runs fine on `core` alone.
#
# WHY this is committed while every other .env is git-ignored: it holds no credentials, only a
# choice about which containers run. Reproducibility beats secrecy here — someone cloning this
# repository should get the same environment you have, and a setting that lives only on your
# machine is a setting nobody else can reproduce (FR-015). The .gitignore carries an explicit
# `!infra/.env` exception for exactly this file.
#
# NOTE: `full` is six services, not the seven the brief lists. Eureka arrives in build step 7,
# because it is a Spring Boot app this project builds rather than a third-party image (T033).

COMPOSE_PROFILES=core
